  80:Drivers/BSP/STM32F429I-Discovery/stm32f429i_discovery_io.c ****   *         necessary hardware resources (GPIOs, clocks..).
  81:Drivers/BSP/STM32F429I-Discovery/stm32f429i_discovery_io.c ****   * @note   BSP_IO_Init() is using HAL_Delay() function to ensure that stmpe811
  82:Drivers/BSP/STM32F429I-Discovery/stm32f429i_discovery_io.c ****   *         IO Expander is correctly reset. HAL_Delay() function provides accurate
  83:Drivers/BSP/STM32F429I-Discovery/stm32f429i_discovery_io.c ****   *         delay (in milliseconds) based on variable incremented in SysTick ISR.
  84:Drivers/BSP/STM32F429I-Discovery/stm32f429i_discovery_io.c ****   *         This implies that if BSP_IO_Init() is called from a peripheral ISR process,
  85:Drivers/BSP/STM32F429I-Discovery/stm32f429i_discovery_io.c ****   *         then the SysTick interrupt must have higher priority (numerically lower)
  86:Drivers/BSP/STM32F429I-Discovery/stm32f429i_discovery_io.c ****   *         than the peripheral interrupt. Otherwise the caller ISR process will be blocked.
  87:Drivers/BSP/STM32F429I-Discovery/stm32f429i_discovery_io.c ****   * @retval IO_OK if all initializations done correctly. Other value if error.
